#!/usr/local/bin/python3.13 -I
"""plans-watch: dated plans from his chats and mails that are not in his calendar or reminders yet -> ONE
~/inbox/vault-plans-*.md per batch, one ack key per plan, so none gets lost in a skimmed or deleted note. No tokens.

Reads the vault's event feed with its own cursor (`vault events --since N --json`: Telegram incl. group chats, and
Gmail; only the facts the vault read from surfaced messages: events by date, to-dos by due date, as anonymized
values, never message text). Each plan (date + time + what) becomes one ledger item. A run:
  - adds new plans (today .. +MAX_DAYS), merges repeats, marks a changed time or date ("was Fri 06.03 18:17");
  - checks dates the vault may have read wrong: a weekday word counted from the message day although the same
    message names its own dates (an itinerary), a day number that does not fit the vault's date ("Freitag, 6."),
    a date the vault masked as an amount ("Do, [amount]."); fixes what it can, flags the rest ("check the date").
    A fact the vault marks `anchored` (it counted the weekday from the message's own earlier date) is taken as is;
    older feed facts and other shapes still get these checks;
  - sorts each plan: sale (ticket pre-sale, registration), deadline (a to-do with a due date), group (a plan or
    invitation in a group chat), proposal (status proposed), plan (his own, confirmed or planned);
  - drops what is already handled: an event in calcache's calendar on that day whose title shares a word with the
    plan (a place word only counts for an event that is not a travel leg), or a reminder (`remind list --json`,
    pending or fired) up to 30 days before it with a shared word;
  - follows a plan after it was noted: a later Telegram message in the same chat with a fact for the same day is
    folded into it (one key per chat and day); a chat with a followed plan in the next WATCH_DAYS days that keeps
    talking is re-read in the vault (`vault --async facts tg CHAT --since DAY`, answers only: once the chat is quiet
    3 min or 15 min after its first new message, at most every 15 min and 8 times a day per chat; the job is
    collected on a later run). A new time, place or participant (or a cancellation) for that day re-lists the plan
    once per change under "Updated", even when it was acked (added/reminded/asked/exists; skipped ones stay quiet);
  - checks each listed plan against calcache for its day: "clashes with <title> HH:MM" for a timed, busy event
    overlapping its time (no end: PLAN_MIN minutes), "in calendar" for its own event (shares a title word or the
    person's first name);
  - shows "Plan with <first name>" (group: "Plan in <chat>") when the vault's title reads like a sentence fragment
    (a relative clause, pronouns, verbs, time words); the ledger keeps the vault's value;
  - writes the note: new and updated plans, plus noted ones nobody acked for 20 h (each at most NOTE_MAX times);
  - a cancelled plan that was acked "added" comes back as "cancelled: fix the calendar".
The note is private (anonymized message data): never forward or quote it. Handling: JOBS.md, skill calendar.

Usage:
  plans-watch run [--cron] [--dry-run] [--seed] [--now ISO]
        --cron: quiet; vault down (`vault health` exit 3) = exit 0, other fetch errors = exit 3 (cron-fail)
        --seed: take in the whole feed (the vault keeps 7 days) as already handled, write no note (first install)
        --dry-run: print the note, change nothing (no re-reads)
  plans-watch open [--json]                 noted plans nobody acked yet (date today or later)
  plans-watch list [--all] [--json]         the ledger (--all: also done, expired, cancelled)
  plans-watch done KEY... --as added|reminded|asked|skipped|exists [--why WORD]
                                            ack: added to the calendar / reminder set / asked him / not his or noise /
                                            was already there; exit 1 = unknown key
  plans-watch reopen KEY                    back to open (it is listed again in the next note)
  plans-watch status [--json]               cursor, last run, counts, updated plans, chat re-reads
Exit: 0 ok, 1 unknown key, 2 usage, 3 fetch or state error.
State: ~/.local/state/vault-events/plans/ (0700; ledger.json 0600; runs.log). The folder stays out of the backup.
Env (tests): PLANS_WATCH_STATE (dir), PLANS_WATCH_INBOX, PLANS_WATCH_CLIENT (vault), PLANS_WATCH_REMIND (remind),
  PLANS_WATCH_CALCACHE (events.json), PLANS_WATCH_NOW (ISO); USAGE=off stops usage events;
  PLANS_WATCH_REFRESH=off: no chat re-reads.
Tests: ~/opt/plans-watch-tests/run.sh
"""
import argparse
